31 files, 3,215 lines.

Where the lines went, which is the part worth looking at:

  answering the question      2049   64%  #########################
  the platform around it       811   25%  ##########
  knowing whether it works     355   11%  ####

The part that answers the question is 64% of the code. Everything
else — 36% of it — is knowing whether the answer was right and
surviving the day the provider is not there. Nobody budgets for that ratio
at the start of a project, and it is the honest reason Parts V and VI exist.

Read it in this order: config, then tools, then agent, then clarity. Four
files and you have the system; the rest is what it took to trust it.
